id.instance: String (TS "c<n>")
num.game: i32
num.cursor: u32
map.ordered: IndexMap
bag.data: IndexMap<String, serde_json::Value>
error.style: Result<_, EngineError> with TS's message; panic only on invariants (refusal strings such as why_choices_refused, why_target_answer_refused are Result<(), EngineError>)
null.optional: Option + skip_serializing_if
null.nullable: Option, serialised null
case.json: camelCase via serde rename_all
case.rust: snake_case
state.mut: &mut GameState writes, &GameState reads, &mut EngineSink for TS sink mutators
rng.source: Rng::new(&state.seed, state.rng_cursor) and write the cursor back
hook.style: Arc<dyn Fn(&mut EffectContext) -> Vec<Effect> + Send + Sync> via hook(); typed hooks via their builders (condition_hook); no fn pointers, no Box
registry.style: OnceLock set once by register_all; fused scripts built on lookup from state; tests use the testkit's thread-local register_catalog/register_scripts
async.style: tokio in crates/server only; none in pure crates
log.style: tracing JSON to stdout, server only
test.live_objects: owned CardInstance copies; re-read with find_instance, write with find_instance_mut
test.sink_for: sink_for(&mut GameState) -> EngineSink<'_>; state read as sink.state while it lives
test.fixture_defs: part 24.6's LazyLock statics read as name.id (PA.bolt.id for an object of defs)
test.default_params: TS defaults passed explicitly (in_hand(.., 1), vanilla_deck(20, 1)); optional -> Option; put options a Value
test.zone_slot: zone functions take &ZoneSlot (as part 24.6's fixtures call them)
test.literals: actions as json! (fixture helpers take impl Serialize) or json_as::<ActionInput>; effect args json_as(json!); toMatchObject via a local matcher over serde_json::Value
test.stage_doubles: testkit::{mock_brittle_tick, mock_animate_at_turn_start, mock_return_at_cleanup}, thread-local (asked of part 31)
